7. UNRESOLVED DISCREPANCIES AT PUBLICATION (open, not hidden)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DISC-049  M7's provenance claim is false in two ways: a7d08a2 is not byte-identical to 8a6e03bb
          (264 files differ, 0 outside developer-review/; 3,553 tracked files there, not 3,806)
          and refs/audit-preserved/base-a7d08a2 does not exist. Recorded; the ref was NOT
          created retroactively.
DISC-050  The modern contact form reports success without sending any request. P1. Open.
DISC-051  The public jobs page requests GET /api/jobs, which is not a registered operation,
          and the registered listing ignores q/location/type. P1. Open.
DISC-052  The create-ticket modal lost Escape handling, focus trap, scroll lock and focus return
          while a Radix Dialog primitive sits unused. P2. Open.
DISC-053  The shared unread-message poller, its backoff ladder and the global unread badge are
          gone; per-page polling stops entirely after one error. P3. Open.
DISC-054  PATCH/archive/restore for enterprise teams call three registry methods that
          MySqlTenantRegistry does not implement (only the in-memory test double does), and
          enterprise_teams has no lead column, so lead assignment cannot persist. The suite is
          green because it runs against the double. P1. Open; predicted failure is 503
          TENANT_TEAM_*_FAILED under MariaDB, stated as predicted, not observed.

Two further items are deliberately left open rather than resolved by assertion:
  * 46 backend test failures are attributed to the absent database; the two residual failures
    (indexes 748, 1112) are labelled residual because the attribution is not proven.
  * Every DOM-level claim in the package, including the three M8 parity reclassifications,
    rests on static reads. The runtime harness (R-01 ... R-10) is the instrument that would
    settle them, and six of its ten scenarios cannot run here.

